","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishantwrp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-07T02:43:38Z","updated_at":"2023-04-20T10:48:44Z","closed_at":"2023-04-20T10:48:44Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-5754](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-5754)\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWe added the 'yb_ysqlserver_connection_over_limit_total' metric to YSQL prometheus endpoint and it is collected at [line of code](https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/blob/master/src/postgres/src/backend/postmaster/postmaster.c#L2337). However, this is not the right place where a connection limit is hit.\r\nPer experiment, the right place is inside each child backend process ([here](https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/blob/master/src/postgres/src/backend/storage/lmgr/proc.c#L348)), rather than in the master process.\r\n\r\nThe right way to implement it should allocate a counter in the shared mem and each time a child process fails due to limit it gets updated. The metric crawler then collects it and sends it to the Prometheus endpoint.\r\n\r\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\r\n\r\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\r\n\r\n[DB-5754]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-5754?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVm